> The essence of this dish is purity—coconut water as the broth, young coconut as both vessel and ingredient, and a free-range chicken for the best results. The coconut milk added at the end creates a silky, slightly creamy broth that coats the chicken beautifully. This is a dish about restraint and letting quality ingredients speak.

== Prepare the Coconut ==

Using a cleaver or large knife, carefully cut the top off a @young coconut{1} (about 1 kg). Save the lid—you'll use it as a serving spoon later.

Strain the @coconut water{400%ml} through a fine mesh sieve into a bowl. Set aside.

Scoop out the @coconut meat{200%g} from the shell with a spoon. Cut into thin strips or small cubes. The younger the coconut, the softer and more jelly-like the meat will be.

== Prepare the Chicken ==

Rinse @chicken pieces{800%g} (thighs and breast, bone-in) and pat dry.

Season with @salt{1%tsp} and @white pepper{½%tsp}. Let rest for ~{10%minutes} to draw out moisture.

== Make the Broth ==

In a large pot, combine the @coconut water{400%ml} and @chicken stock{400%ml}. Bring to a boil over medium heat.

Add the @chicken pieces{800%g}, skin-side up. The liquid should just barely cover the chicken.

Reduce heat to a gentle simmer—never let the broth boil vigorously or the chicken will become tough. Skim any foam that rises to the surface.

Add @ginger{3%slices} and @scallions{2%stalks}. Cover and simmer for ~{25%minutes} until the chicken is cooked through and tender. A chopstick should easily pierce the thickest part of the thigh.

== Finish the Soup ==

Remove the chicken pieces and set aside. Strain the broth through a fine mesh sieve into a clean pot.

Return the broth to a simmer. Stir in @coconut milk{120%ml} and the @coconut meat{200%g}.

Taste and adjust seasoning with @salt{to taste} and @white pepper{few%grains}.

== Serve ==

Divide the @coconut meat{200%g} among serving bowls. Ladle the hot broth over the coconut.

Place the cooked chicken pieces on top. The residual heat will warm the coconut without cooking it further, preserving its texture.

Garnish with @coriander{10%g} or @chives{5%g} (optional).

Serve in the coconut shells if you have extras, or in wide soup bowls with chopsticks and a spoon.